    "body": "Thanks for raising this, this happens to be exactly what I'm working on in the WebKit implementation right now and came to a similar conclusion that what the spec says right now is broken and what browsers do is also broken. Specifically I agree with your proposed behaviour for when moveBefore() is involved.\n\nOne extra spanner in the works that I've been looking at is what happens when you have a form control that is associated with a form via (I think) the foster parenting steps.\n\n```html\n<table><form id=\"parser-form-1\"><tr><td><input id=\"parser-input-1\"></td></tr></form></table>\n```\n\nIn cases like this, we need to decide what happens when you move the input, and when you move the form itself, and when you move the containing table. I think to match existing browsers (and match what I think is reasonable), we need to pass extra data from the DOM spec, see https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1519\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
