    "body": "I'm not overly wedded to one way of doing things so @domenic if your DOM PR for example patches more than my one I'm happy to close mine and go with yours. Yours does seem to do more iterating but I understand that's because of \"an ancestor’s hooks can change a descendant’s form owner. Keep custom element upgrade handling at its existing point in insertion.\".?\n\nFrom what I can tell though browsers don't actually do the subtree first behaviour they do the per node behaviour.",
